"$\vec r=\mu(2\hat i-\hat j+2\hat k),\ \mu\ge0$" → used $\vec d_2=(2,-1,2)$ correctly → MATCHES; 
"L3 is perpendicular to both $R_1$ and $R_2$ and cuts both of them" → interpreted “cuts both” as “passes through a common point of $R_1$ and $R_2$” → MISMATCH.

